# quantity  mode  [C, floor in units of machine epsilon]
# common envelope: adiabatic, self-gravity + 2 sinks, global timesteps
# the treecode conserves linear and angular momentum exactly, so these are enforced to round-off.
# The centre of mass moves uniformly (snapshot has non-zero momentum) and is checked after removing
# that motion; round-off in summing m*x over 8e5 particles with ejecta at large radius is
# ~eps*sqrt(N)*R_max ~ 1e-10, hence the larger C. A secular drift would exceed this quickly.
etot   ref
totmom exact
angtot exact
xcom   exact 5e6
ycom   exact 5e6
zcom   exact 5e6
